// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`discoverability (OSS_SPEC §12) > --debug-agent lists logs, config precedence and every env var 1`] = `
"storage-server 0.1.0 troubleshooting context
node <v>

Logs:
  debug log (always on, plain text, one line per event, appended): /xdg/state/storage-server/debug.log
  terminal output mirrors status/warn/error lines; add --debug (or STORAGE_DEBUG=1) for debug lines on stderr
  the tamper-evident audit log lives in the database: storage-server audit tail

Configuration precedence: flags > environment > config.json > defaults
  data dir: /xdg/data/storage-server
  config file: /xdg/data/storage-server/config.json (JSON, same keys as the server config)

Environment variables:
  STORAGE_DATA_DIR: Directory holding the database, blobs, certificates and config.json.
  STORAGE_DEBUG: Also print debug-level log lines to stderr.
  STORAGE_NAME: Display name shown in pairing QR codes and /v1/info.
  STORAGE_PUBLIC_URL: Externally reachable base URL devices use, e.g. https://home.example.org or https://203.0.113.7:443.
  STORAGE_APP_URL: Wrap QR payloads as <app-url>#oss=… so a phone camera opens the app directly.
  STORAGE_HOST: Address to listen on.
  STORAGE_PORT: HTTPS (or plain HTTP with --tls off) port.
  STORAGE_HTTP_PORT: Plain-HTTP port for ACME http-01 challenges and HTTPS redirects (0 = any free port; unset = disabled).
  STORAGE_ADMIN_PORT: Admin console port (-1 disables).
  STORAGE_ADMIN_HOST: Interface the admin console listens on. Keep it on loopback. Only in a container with published ports use 0.0.0.0, published as -p 127.0.0.1:8081:8081.
  STORAGE_REMOTE_CONSOLE: Let admin devices (paired with \`pair --console\` or from the console) use the admin console remotely at /v1/console. Inert until one is paired.
  STORAGE_TLS: How HTTPS certificates are obtained.
  STORAGE_DOMAINS: DNS name or public IP to certify (repeatable; env is comma-separated).
  STORAGE_ACME_EMAIL: Contact address for the ACME account.
  STORAGE_ACME_DIRECTORY: ACME directory URL (use the staging URL while testing).
  STORAGE_ACME_PROFILE: ACME certificate profile; defaults to shortlived when an IP is certified.
  STORAGE_CERT_FILE: PEM certificate chain (with --tls files).
  STORAGE_KEY_FILE: PEM private key (with --tls files).
  STORAGE_UPNP: Forward the ports on the home router via UPnP IGD or NAT-PMP.
  STORAGE_UPNP_LEASE: Port-mapping lease; renewed at half-life.
  STORAGE_TRUST_PROXY: Trust X-Forwarded-For from a reverse proxy (only behind one).
  STORAGE_CORS: CORS policy: origins learnt at pairing (plus --cors-origin), or any origin.
  STORAGE_CORS_ORIGINS: Always-allowed app origin (repeatable; env is comma-separated).
  STORAGE_DEFAULT_QUOTA: Storage quota for new non-admin accounts (unset = unlimited).
  STORAGE_HISTORY_DAYS: Keep earlier versions of a file this many days after they were replaced (0 = none). The console's Settings can change it at runtime.
  STORAGE_HISTORY_VERSIONS: Keep at most this many versions of each file.
  STORAGE_TRASH_DAYS: Keep deleted files in the trash this many days.
  STORAGE_LOG_FILE: Path of the always-on debug log file.
  XDG_DATA_HOME: Base for the default data directory.
  XDG_STATE_HOME: Base for the default log directory.

Common failures and how to diagnose them:
  devices cannot connect           -> storage-server doctor --public-url <url>; curl -v <url>/v1/info
  certificate errors in the app    -> storage-server cert status (acme: check --domain and that port 80 or 443 is reachable)
  port forwarding does not work    -> storage-server upnp status (CGNAT / double NAT is reported explicitly)
  'origin not allowed' in browser  -> the app origin was never paired: pair from that origin or add --cors-origin
  401 after an app update          -> the device was revoked or its account disabled: storage-server devices list
  database or audit problems       -> storage-server audit verify; storage-server doctor
  data looks stale on a device     -> the app pulls /v1/ns/<id>/changes; a 410 means the device must resync

Capture a reproducer: run with --debug, reproduce, then attach the debug log and \`storage-server doctor\` output.
Never attach the data dir: it contains the (encrypted) data and the TLS private key."
`;

exports[`discoverability (OSS_SPEC §12) > --help-agent is deterministic and points at \`commands\` 1`] = `
"storage-server 0.1.0: a self-hosted, zero-knowledge storage server for local-first PWAs built on @niclaslindstedt/oss-framework.
Apps encrypt everything on the device; the server stores ciphertext files and rows per namespace, detects conflicts atomically,
keeps history and a trash, streams change events, shares single namespaces between accounts, pairs devices by QR code,
gets its own HTTPS certificates (ACME) and forwards router ports (UPnP / NAT-PMP).

Commands:
  serve: Run the storage server (the default command).
  setup: Create the first admin pairing and print its QR code.
  pair: Print a one-time QR code that enrols a device.
  accounts: List, create, update and delete accounts.
  devices: List and revoke devices.
  namespaces: List namespaces (metadata only — contents are end-to-end encrypted).
  audit: Verify or read the tamper-evident audit log.
  backup: Write a consistent copy of the data directory.
  cert: Show or renew the TLS certificate.
  upnp: Inspect or change router port forwarding.
  doctor: Check the installation end to end.
  admin: Print the admin console sign-in link, or rotate its token.
  health: Probe the local server (for container and service health checks).
  test-server: Run an in-memory server in test mode (for end-to-end tests).
  commands: List commands in a stable, grep-friendly format.
  docs: Print an embedded documentation topic.
  man: Print an embedded manual page.

Most important flags:
  --data-dir: Directory holding the database, blobs, certificates and config.json. (env STORAGE_DATA_DIR)
  --tls: How HTTPS certificates are obtained. (env STORAGE_TLS)
  --domain: DNS name or public IP to certify (repeatable; env is comma-separated). (env STORAGE_DOMAINS)
  --port: HTTPS (or plain HTTP with --tls off) port. (env STORAGE_PORT)
  --http-port: Plain-HTTP port for ACME http-01 challenges and HTTPS redirects (0 = any free port; unset = disabled). (env STORAGE_HTTP_PORT)
  --upnp: Forward the ports on the home router via UPnP IGD or NAT-PMP. (env STORAGE_UPNP)
  --public-url: Externally reachable base URL devices use, e.g. https://home.example.org or https://203.0.113.7:443. (env STORAGE_PUBLIC_URL)

Discover more (recommended for agents):
  storage-server commands                  # every command, one per line
  storage-server commands pair             # full flag/exit-code spec of one command
  storage-server commands --examples       # example invocations
  storage-server man <command>             # reference manual page
  storage-server docs [topic]              # embedded guides (getting started, home hosting, security, protocol)
  storage-server --debug-agent             # troubleshooting context"
`;
